<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI names Memphis top air cargo airport in May.</title>
<headline>ACI names Memphis top air cargo airport in May.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in May 1996,  said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The airport handled 173,829 tonnes of cargo in the month in question, up 23.5 percent on May 1995.</p>
<p>Occupying second-place in the ACI table of top cargo-handling airports was Los Angeles, reporting 143,451 tonnes, up 11.9 percent on the previous year's levels.</p>
<p>In third place was Miami, which handled 139,287 tonnes. The airport ranked third place despite a decrease of 0.1 percent on May 1995.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in May 1996, with the volume they handled, the percentage change over May 1995 and, in parentheses, their May 1995 ranking, were as follows:</p>
<p>	   City		   Tonnes	    Percentage change</p>
<p>							  from a year ago.</p>
<p> 1  (1)  Memphis		173,829 tonnes  (up   23.5)</p>
<p> 2  (5)  Los Angeles	  143,451 tonnes  (up   11.9)</p>
<p> 3  (2)  Miami		  139,287 tonnes  (down  0.1)</p>
<p> 4  (4)  New York	     133,964 tonnes  (up    3.9)</p>
<p> 5  (6)  Hong Kong	    131,200 tonnes  (up    4.9)</p>
<p> 6  (3)  Tokyo		  127,228 tonnes  (down  5.2)</p>
<p> 7  (7)  Frankfurt	    121,146 tonnes  (up    5.9)</p>
<p> 8  (8)  Louisville	   115,836 tonnes  (up    5.8)</p>
<p> 9  (10) Seoul		  111,468 tonnes  (up   15.6)</p>
<p> 10 (9)  Chicago		104,882 tonnes  (up    1.9)</p>
<p> 11 (14) Anchorage	    101,758 tonnes  (up   30.0)</p>
<p> 12 (12) Singapore	     98,439 tonnes  (up    8.4)</p>
<p> 13 (11) London Heathrow     96,369 tonnes  (up    2.3)</p>
<p> 14 (13) Amsterdam	     89,859 tonnes  (up   12.5)</p>
<p> 15 (15) New York Newark     85,599 tonnes  (up   11.5)</p>
<p> 16 (16) Paris-CDG	     76,082 tonnes  (up    2.3)</p>
<p> 17 (19) Atlanta		 69,441 tonnes  (up   13.8)</p>
<p> 18 (18) Dallas Fort Worth   67,089 tonnes  (up    7.1)</p>
<p> 19 (-)  Dayton		  66,107 tonnes  (up   38.2)</p>
<p> 20 (17) Taipei		  65,878 tonnes  (down  3.2)</p>
